 "script": "A I data centers were on forty-five local ballots Tuesday. Thirty-three measures to limit them passed, Engadget and Tom's Hardware reported. They range from outright bans to pauses and energy caps. Here's why it matters to you. Many residents worry data centers will push up their power bills. Wall Street noticed. On Wednesday, the Nasdaq fell three percent as investors sold tech stocks. The Associated Press says traders fear data center pauses in some areas. Some towns now want a public vote before one gets built. What would make you accept a data center near your home? Tell us below.",
